  "body": "See https://github.com/mikewest/corpp/pull/2\r\n\r\nOnce Structured Headers is more stable, the COEP and COOP headers should be parsed as SH \"item\", and unknown parameters should be ignored (without ignoring the entire value).\r\n\r\nCurrently, [COOP](https://gist.github.com/annevk/6f2dd8c79c77123f39797f6bdac43f3e) is specified as comparing the whole value, and COEP (as of https://github.com/mikewest/corpp/pull/2 ) is specified in terms of SH but any parameter causes the entire value to be ignored. (I believe these two are equivalent.)\r\n\r\ncc @annevk @domenic @mikewest @mnot",
